    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **68 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>` (no separators), and removed the standalone `checkDigit`.\n\n**New/changed core logic**\n- **`MemberId.java`** (new) \u2014 builds the id (`region + fy2 + hash8 + Luhn-CHK` computed over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`) and parses the region / 2-digit FY back out of an id. Region is read as the leading letter-run and FY as the two digits after it, so parsing tolerates the `-<n>` collision suffix.\n- **`AssignMemberId.java`** (new, replaces `AssignCustomerCode`) \u2014 assigns `memberId` after `BuildOwner`, with collision de-duplication now applied to the whole `memberId`.\n- Deleted **`AssignCustomerCode.java`** and **`AssignMembershipNumber.java`**.\n\n**Downstream consumers now reference `memberId`**\n- **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit` mapping; `deriveLocality` (feeding locality/timezone/**ownerSegment**) now reads the region from `memberId`; a new `deriveFiscalYear` reads the **FY** from `memberId` (falling back to the registration date for legacy rows).\n- **`AuditOwnerCreated`** \u2014 the audit line now logs `memberId` (plus id, registrationDate, membershipLevel).\n- **`AuditOwnerCreatedEvent`** \u2014 the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event's primary identifier is now `memberId`.\n\n**Schema & contract**\n- **`Owner`** model: `memberId` field/accessors replace `customerCode` + `membershipNumber`.\n- **`owners.POST.yml`**: `assignCode`\u2192`assignMemberId`; removed the `assignMembership` step.\n- **`openapi.yml`**: `memberId` property replaces `customerCode`/`checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` (DTOs are generated from this).\n- **schema.sql** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres): single `member_id` column replaces `customer_code` + `membership_number`.\n\nExample generated ids from the run: `NSW267D0C08EF1`, `UNKNOWN26B773B4184`.",
